<p><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>So the=
 logic
is:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><strong><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif";
font-weight:normal;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold'>Store values &#8594; Calculate
average &#8594; Compare each value with average &#8594; Print above-average
days</span></strong><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sa=
ns-serif"'>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>Questi=
on 6:
Explain why the program crashes on an empty string input and describe the c=
heck
your pointer-based solution must perform before dereferencing the pointer. =
How
does traversing a string using a pointer differ from traversing it using ar=
ray
index notation, and which approach makes the empty-input bug easier to catc=
h?<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif";font-w=
eight:
normal;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold'>Answer<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>The pr=
ogram
crashes on an <strong><span style=3D'font-family:"Arial","sans-serif";font-=
weight:
normal;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold'>empty string</span></strong> because ther=
e is
no character to safely access. If the code dereferences a pointer without
checking whether the string contains a character, it may access invalid mem=
ory.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif";font-w=
eight:
normal;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold'>Pointer check<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>Before
dereferencing the pointer, check that it is not <code inline=3D""><span
style=3D'mso-ansi-font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"A=
rial","sans-serif"'>NULL</span></code>
and that the string is not empty:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<pre><span class=3DGramE><code><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:=
"Arial","sans-serif"'>if</span></code></span><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'> (<span class=
=3DSpellE>str</span> !=3D NULL &amp;&amp; *<span
class=3DSpellE>str</span> !=3D '\0')<o:p></o:p></span></code></pre><pre><co=
de><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>{<o:p></o:p></s=
pan></code></pre><pre><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><span style=3D'=
mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span>// Safe to use *<span
class=3DSpellE><span class=3DGramE>str</span></span><o:p></o:p></span></cod=
e></pre><pre><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>}</span></code>=
<span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><o:p></o:p></sp=
an></pre>

<p><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>Here, =
<code
inline=3D""><span style=3D'mso-ansi-font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.=
0pt;
font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>'\0'</span></code> represents the <strong=
><span
style=3D'font-family:"Arial","sans-serif";font-weight:normal;mso-bidi-font-=
weight:
bold'>end of the string</span></strong>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<h3><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif";font-w=
eight:
normal;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold'>Pointer vs. array indexing<o:p></o:p></sp=
an></h3>

<p><strong><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif";
font-weight:normal;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold'>Array indexing:</span></stron=
g><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><o:p></o:p></sp=
an></p>

<pre><span class=3DGramE><code><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:=
"Arial","sans-serif"'>for</span></code></span><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'> (i =3D 0; <span
class=3DSpellE>str</span>[i] !=3D '\0'; i++)<o:p></o:p></span></code></pre>=
<pre><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>{<o:p></o:p></s=
pan></code></pre><pre><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><span style=3D'=
mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span><span
class=3DSpellE><span class=3DGramE>printf</span></span><span class=3DGramE>=
(</span>&quot;%c&quot;, <span
class=3DSpellE>str</span>[i]);<o:p></o:p></span></code></pre><pre><code><sp=
an
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>}</span></code>=
<span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><o:p></o:p></sp=
an></pre>

<p><strong><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif";
font-weight:normal;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold'>Pointer traversal:</span></st=
rong><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><o:p></o:p></sp=
an></p>

<pre><span class=3DGramE><code><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:=
"Arial","sans-serif"'>char</span></code></span><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'> *p =3D <span
class=3DSpellE>str</span>;<o:p></o:p></span></code></pre><pre><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:=
p></span></code></pre><pre><span
class=3DGramE><code><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sa=
ns-serif"'>while</span></code></span><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'> (p !=3D NULL &=
amp;&amp; *p !=3D '\0')<o:p></o:p></span></code></pre><pre><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>{<o:p></o:p></s=
pan></code></pre><pre><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><span style=3D'=
mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span><span
class=3DSpellE><span class=3DGramE>printf</span></span><span class=3DGramE>=
(</span>&quot;%c&quot;, *p);<o:p></o:p></span></code></pre><pre><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><span style=3D'=
mso-spacerun:yes'>    </span><span
class=3DGramE>p</span>++;<o:p></o:p></span></code></pre><pre><code><span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>}</span></code>=
<span
style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><o:p></o:p></sp=
an></pre>

<p><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>With a=
rray
indexing, we access characters using <span class=3DSpellE><span class=3DGra=
mE><code
inline=3D""><span style=3D'mso-ansi-font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.=
0pt;
font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>str</span></code></span></span><span
class=3DGramE><code><span style=3D'mso-ansi-font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-=
size:
14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>[</span></code></span><code><span
style=3D'mso-ansi-font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"A=
rial","sans-serif"'>i]</span></code>.
With pointers, we access the current character using <code inline=3D""><span
style=3D'mso-ansi-font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"A=
rial","sans-serif"'>*p</span></code>
and move to the next character using <code inline=3D""><span style=3D'mso-a=
nsi-font-size:
14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'>p++</spa=
n></code>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><strong><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif";
font-weight:normal;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold'>Array indexing is generally
easier for beginners to understand and makes the empty-string condition more
obvious</span></strong><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial",=
"sans-serif"'>,
because the loop directly checks <span class=3DSpellE><code inline=3D""><sp=
an
style=3D'mso-ansi-font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"A=
rial","sans-serif"'>str</span></code></span><code><span
style=3D'mso-ansi-font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"A=
rial","sans-serif"'>[i<span
class=3DGramE>] !</span>=3D '\0'</span></code>. However, both approaches ar=
e safe
if the empty-string case is checked correctly.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p><span style=3D'font-size:14.0pt;font-family:"Arial","sans-serif"'><o:p>&=
nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

